From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shawn-makes-stuff <shawn.rains@rocketmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:54:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/20] rusticc: COSMOS host patches (configfile, logging,
 thermistor, probe, shaper, load cell)

- 0001-remove-save-config-subfile-check: no autosave strip on load, no
  include conflict check on SAVE_CONFIG
- 0004-allow-config-exclude: [!section] removes a defined section
- 0001-Reduce-log-rotate-threshold: queuelogger rotates by size (python 3.15
  RotatingFileHandler, 5 MiB, 2 backups)
- 0001-implement-pulldown-resistor-in-thermistor-calc: pulldown_resistor on
  thermistors and custom thermistors
- 0001-probe-home-z-includes-z-offset, 0001-force-specific-input-shaper
  (FORCE_SHAPER), 0002-reduce-calibration-difference-tolerance (0.1 %)

Verified: rusticc/cases cosmos + cosmos_exclude_bad identical to the COSMOS
reference (full set 151/152, printers/13 timing as before); unit tests of
calc_temp/calc_adc with pulldown against COSMOS's python, and of the size
rollover.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
